I've been working today.

00:00:26.174 --> 00:00:28.134
It's actually closer to 16.

00:00:28.134 --> 00:00:29.542
- [Voiceover] Iwona asks,

00:00:29.542 --> 00:00:31.389
"What would you do if you
were in your dad's shoes

00:00:31.389 --> 00:00:34.931
"and you didn't come to
the US until you were 23?"

00:00:34.931 --> 00:00:36.265
- You know, Iwona,

00:00:36.265 --> 00:00:39.306
I want to believe that if I came to the US

00:00:39.306 --> 00:00:40.827
in the way that my dad did,

00:00:40.827 --> 00:00:42.626
which was not only at 23 years old,

00:00:42.626 --> 00:00:44.971
but also with a child and
another one on the way,

00:00:44.971 --> 00:00:46.631
that I would do the
same thing that he did,

00:00:46.631 --> 00:00:49.162
which was completely work
his face off to allow

00:00:49.162 --> 00:00:51.589
the next generation to kind
of build on top of that,

00:00:51.589 --> 00:00:53.051
and so, you know,

00:00:53.051 --> 00:00:57.410
I don't think I would've
done anything different.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:58.592
I think a lot of it's circumstance.

00:00:58.592 --> 00:01:01.553
My dad had a great uncle
who had a liquor store

00:01:01.553 --> 00:01:02.689
that he got to work in.

00:01:02.689 --> 00:01:04.129
That great uncle passed away

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:05.871
and it was just all these
kind of different variables.

00:01:05.871 --> 00:01:07.995
I think circumstance has a lot to do with

00:01:07.995 --> 00:01:09.516
what I would've done,

00:01:09.516 --> 00:01:11.094
but the one thing I
know I would've done is

00:01:11.094 --> 00:01:15.206
work every hour of every day.

00:01:15.206 --> 00:01:16.473
- [Voiceover] Tommy asks,

00:01:16.473 --> 00:01:18.529
"In 13 thoughts of being an entrepreneur,

00:01:18.529 --> 00:01:22.069
"you say you focus on top
line versus bottom line. Why?"

00:01:22.069 --> 00:01:23.369
- Tommy, you know,

00:01:23.369 --> 00:01:25.250
one thing I think a lot
of entrepreneurs do,

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.608
especially ones that are
just starting companies,

00:01:26.608 --> 00:01:28.094
since I invest in so many of them,

00:01:28.094 --> 00:01:29.313
that completely blows me away

00:01:29.313 --> 00:01:32.140
is they start looking to drive margin,

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:34.131
profit very early on.

00:01:34.131 --> 00:01:36.123
The reason I always focus
on top line revenue,

00:01:36.123 --> 00:01:38.434
and it was something I
did in my dad's business

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:40.800
and something that AJ felt
when I started going full time

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.712
on the Vayner front was
you can always drive

00:01:43.712 --> 00:01:45.580
your profits higher eventually,

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:46.909
but when you cut a moment in time,

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:49.706
and when I run businesses,
I tend to innovate,

00:01:49.706 --> 00:01:52.447
and I tend to be slightly
ahead of the market,

00:01:52.447 --> 00:01:55.511
and the market eventually
catches up to me,

00:01:55.511 --> 00:01:56.959
and then that's the good thing.

00:01:56.959 --> 00:01:58.236
That's the moment when it gets exciting.

00:01:58.236 --> 00:02:00.159
People start believing
in social media marketing

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:02.561
or believing in internet
e-commerce wine businesses

00:02:02.561 --> 00:02:07.539
or believing in Australian, New
Zealand, South African wine,

00:02:07.539 --> 00:02:10.827
I have to really run fast
and grab as many customers

00:02:10.827 --> 00:02:12.208
because I'm slightly ahead.

00:02:12.208 --> 00:02:14.079
Then three, four, five, six,

00:02:14.079 --> 00:02:15.669
seven, eight years down the line,

00:02:15.669 --> 00:02:16.422
I can start driving profit.

00:02:16.422 --> 00:02:18.442
You can always start cutting costs

00:02:18.442 --> 00:02:21.309
and raising prices at any time,

00:02:21.309 --> 00:02:23.341
but land grabbing more customers

00:02:23.341 --> 00:02:25.501
gives you leverage of the scale

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.346
that you ultimately need to convert them,

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:30.202
and so I think people go
in for the right hook,

00:02:30.202 --> 00:02:33.499
the big right hook a lot
of times way too early,

00:02:33.499 --> 00:02:35.449
sometimes to appease investors,

00:02:35.449 --> 00:02:37.829
sometimes because they just
want to start buying boats

00:02:37.829 --> 00:02:39.226
and Rolexes,

00:02:39.226 --> 00:02:42.520
and I'm just kind of pushing
and building leverage

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.412
for the long term.

00:02:44.412 --> 00:02:46.060
- Hey, Gary. John Lee Dumas,

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.337
Entrepreneur on Fire here,

00:02:47.337 --> 00:02:50.320
and I have a #AskGaryVee question.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:53.792
Pareto's Law states that 80
percent of our desired outcomes

00:02:53.792 --> 00:02:57.042
come from just 20 percent
of our activities.

00:02:57.042 --> 00:02:58.342
Do you agree with this?

00:02:58.342 --> 00:03:01.175
If so, what's your 20?

00:03:01.175 --> 00:03:01.985
- That's a great question.

00:03:01.985 --> 00:03:04.864
I think a lot of people
have brought that up.

00:03:04.864 --> 00:03:07.000
I know a lot of people in our
organization believe in that.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.660
I've heard a lot of
people believe in that.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.329
You know, do I believe in
that and what is my 20?

00:03:11.329 --> 00:03:14.529
John, first of all,
congrats on your podcast.

00:03:17.119 --> 00:03:19.301
I probably think weirdly enough

00:03:19.301 --> 00:03:21.104
that it might even be more extreme.

00:03:21.104 --> 00:03:22.311
There's a big part of me that thinks

00:03:22.311 --> 00:03:24.471
it's probably closer to 98 and two.

00:03:24.471 --> 00:03:25.898
Then there's another part of me

00:03:25.898 --> 00:03:28.488
that believes it's two and 98.

00:03:28.488 --> 00:03:31.412
I am the kind of person
that doesn't give a crap

00:03:31.412 --> 00:03:34.152
about other people's laws or principles.

00:03:34.152 --> 00:03:36.371
What feels right for me is execution.

00:03:36.371 --> 00:03:38.704
I think when people start knowing...

00:03:38.704 --> 00:03:39.830
This is kind of what I talk about,

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:43.521
my naivety or lack of knowledge helps me.

00:03:43.521 --> 00:03:45.529
I think if I knew about this law

00:03:45.529 --> 00:03:47.051
prior to you bringing it up...

00:03:47.051 --> 00:03:48.513
I mean, I've heard about the 80/20 rule,

00:03:48.513 --> 00:03:49.830
but I didn't know the official name.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:50.933
If I knew about this law,

00:03:50.933 --> 00:03:53.952
it would actually make we
want to play within that law,

00:03:53.952 --> 00:03:55.948
and then that would probably
take away from the strength

00:03:55.948 --> 00:03:57.192
that I create every day.

00:03:57.192 --> 00:03:59.687
People asked me what the ROI
of the #AskGaryVee show is

00:03:59.687 --> 00:04:00.731
a couple episodes ago.

00:04:00.731 --> 00:04:02.067
You hardcore watchers know,

00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:04.701
and I say, "Well, this is
selling my fourth book."

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:05.913
Here's what I think.

00:04:05.913 --> 00:04:09.012
I think human beings
overthink shit, right?

00:04:09.012 --> 00:04:10.928
And try to buy into some sort of thesis,

00:04:10.928 --> 00:04:12.274
read a book that makes them feel good,

00:04:12.274 --> 00:04:14.934
whether it's Crush It! or Pareto's Law,

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:15.977
or whatever it's called,

00:04:15.977 --> 00:04:18.427
and I think that is a fundamental problem.

00:04:18.427 --> 00:04:20.934
I think when we start
coming from what's authentic

00:04:20.934 --> 00:04:22.515
and what feels more natural...

00:04:22.515 --> 00:04:24.115
You know, the law I believe in

00:04:24.115 --> 00:04:26.194
is that my mom and dad
had sex at a moment,

00:04:26.194 --> 00:04:29.653
created me, and I'm taking
this DNA to the finish line.

00:04:29.653 --> 00:04:30.408
That law.

00:04:30.408 --> 00:04:32.295
That's the law I believe in.

